<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bunkeya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bunkeya is a town in Haut-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/katanga">Katanga</a> province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>. In the second half of the 19th century it was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/msiri">Msiri</a>'s Yeke kingdom, a great trading centre for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves. The Scottish missionary Frederick Arnot settled there in 1886, and Msiri was killed at Bunkeya by an officer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stairs-expedition-to-katanga">Stairs Expedition</a> in December 1891.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bunkeya.jpg" alt="Bunkeya" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rexparry sydney · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stairs_Expedition_Map_lo-res.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
